# >>> squiddy-generated graph ignore rules (DN-056 R-250) >>>
# The kit's ignore rules for one graph (SQ-111, DN-056 R-250): the kit repository's `graphs/*/` block, scoped to this
# directory, so the kit and every consumer agree. TRACKED: the manifest, candidates, allow-list and abstentions, the
# ledger, the spec and configs, the factory's controls, incidents, questions and intake lists, the export index. NOT
# TRACKED: bytes and regenerable state. A pattern that may name a symlink has NO trailing slash: `texts/` matches only a
# directory, so a link named `texts` was committed with its absolute target (SQ-109 row 5).
corpus/*
!corpus/manifest.yaml
!corpus/candidates/
!corpus/manifest_property_allowlist.yaml
!corpus/identifier_abstentions.jsonl
ledger/*.bak-*
ledger/snapshots
exports/*.json
exports/*.jsonl
evidence/*/*.rows.jsonl
evidence/*/wordlists
work
work_*.log
texts
pilot/work
extract/records
extract/raw
extract/meter.jsonl
extract/daemon.log
extract/daemon.pid
extract/control.json
extract/state.json
extract/daemon.lock
extract/ingested.json
extract/pilot_gate.json
extract/ingest_gate.json
extract/checkpoints
extract/protocol_gate
extract/protocol_gate_*.json
factory/*
!factory/control.yaml
!factory/incidents/
!factory/questions_operator.md
!factory/intake/
STOP
# A hand-dropped file's bytes never enter a repository (R-212's inbox; DN-034 R-158: a held text leaves the machine
# only under a licence the graph allows). The directory is kept by its `.gitkeep`. A file a worktree's removal deletes
# is now a named refusal before the next write (R-249); an inbox declared under the archive root (`dir: archive:inbox`)
# survives every checkout.
intake/inbox/*
!intake/inbox/.gitkeep
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# <<< squiddy-generated graph ignore rules <<<
